_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexhalbi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would say having them as two seperate options is prettier, so I would opt for the first option.\r\nIf none is set we have the behaviour we have right now. If one is set it is just using IPv4 or IPv6, if both are set the client can choose.\r\n\r\n\r\nI thought about getting them dynamically too, but that could be a problem, when the IP changes via DNS. I do not know if the DERP-Map is actually cached in Headscale and what happens if it is overridden with an internal IP on Headscale itself. So I thought better to simply add them to the config. \r\n\r\nIt could be done dynamically though like in bootstrap-DNS: https://github.com/alexhalbi/headscale/blob/6e734bc864abc13f8d608cb7e566611bf9593b2f/hscontrol/derp/server/derp_server.go#L228\r\n```go\r\naddrs, err := resolver.LookupIP(resolvCtx, \"ip\", node.HostName)\r\n```\r\nIt could be added here: https://github.com/alexhalbi/headscale/blob/6e734bc864abc13f8d608cb7e566611bf9593b2f/hscontrol/derp/server/derp_server.go#L86","created_at":"2023-09-29T16:17:05Z","updated_at":"2023-09-29T16:21:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1565#discussion_r1341567757","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/comments/1341567757"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1565#discussion_r1341567757"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1565"}},"r